<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The app's paper background, matching the bg custom property in globals.css.

        Capacitor 8's SystemBars plugin pads the WebView's parent by the system
        bar insets whenever the device's WebView is older than version 140 —
        older WebViews get the CSS safe-area insets wrong, so it insets the view
        instead and reports the safe area as zero. That padding is what showed
        as a white band above the header and below the nav: the CoordinatorLayout
        behind the WebView had no background, so the window's default light grey
        showed through.

        Painting it the app's own paper closes the gap on those devices, and is
        invisible on newer WebViews, where Capacitor passes the insets through
        and the WebView genuinely fills the screen.
    -->
    <color name="pondPaper">#F5F2EB</color>
</resources>
